        "loc_mini_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dark venomous snakes have poison path dao marks, and their snake guts are treated as top immortal material for refining healing Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1241
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dark-venomous-snakes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_dark_venomous_snake",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After a heavenly tribulation of five poisonous beasts, Fang Yuan uses perceivable dao Immortal Gu and finds he gained about a thousand poison path dao marks, above the usual seven hundred and fifty from a heavenly tribulation. From then on, poison path Immortal Gu gain a hundred percent amplification for him. Heaven’s will chose poison path while he had almost no poison foundation beyond Woman’s Heart, so the marks did little to speed his growth.",
      "chapters": [
        1470
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribulation-amplification",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_perceivable_dao_immortal_gu",
        "sys_heavens_will",
        "gu_womans_heart"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Beast digesting rotten qi holds dense poison path dao marks. It does not affect desolate plants, variant humans, or pure humans. It only thins wild beasts and can dissolve the skin and organs of immemorial desolate beasts.",
      "chapters": [
        1706
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "beast-digesting-rotten-qi",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When an immortal aperture gains poison path dao marks, plagues or diseases that were seasonal may erupt instead and spread widely and rapidly.",
      "chapters": [
        2109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "plague-risk-in-apertures",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rotten Mud Mountain has poison path dao marks, but it mostly contains earth path dao marks, and mud Gu materials suit feeding the mud monster Ni Jian.",
      "chapters": [
        2128
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
